1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:05,150
What makes JEI Math different from
other math learning programs?

2
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:09,624
Let's explore three key strengths
of JEI Math: comprehensive

3
00:00:09,687 --> 00:00:13,083
mathematical content, systematic
learning progression,

4
00:00:13,146 --> 00:00:16,480
and precise diagnosis and
personalized prescriptions.

5
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:20,931
What makes a difference in math learning

6
00:00:20,982 --> 00:00:23,340
isn't simply how many
problems students solve.

7
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:27,010
What truly matters is what
students learn, how they learn,

8
00:00:27,063 --> 00:00:30,450
and how their individual learning
levels and needs are assessed.

9
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:36,080
JEI Math stands out in three key ways.

10
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:41,490
First, it covers all five major areas of
mathematics, going beyond arithmetic.

11
00:00:42,090 --> 00:00:46,136
Second, it provides a systematic
learning progression, from understanding

12
00:00:46,192 --> 00:00:50,460
mathematical concepts and principles to
applying them and developing mastery.

13
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:55,319
Third, it analyzes learning gaps and
possible causes of errors from multiple

14
00:00:55,375 --> 00:00:59,970
perspectives to provide precise diagnosis
and personalized learning prescriptions.

15
00:01:02,370 --> 00:01:05,840
The first difference lies in the
range of mathematical content.

16
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:13,010
Program A primarily focuses on numbers
and operations, from basic arithmetic

17
00:01:13,072 --> 00:01:17,340
with whole numbers to calculations
involving fractions and decimals.

18
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:21,692
Through repeated practice, from
basic to more complex calculations,

19
00:01:21,748 --> 00:01:24,940
it emphasizes improving
computational accuracy and speed.

20
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:30,158
While this approach helps students develop
computational fluency, its emphasis on

21
00:01:30,214 --> 00:01:34,955
numbers and operations provides less exposure
to other areas of mathematics, limiting

22
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:39,640
opportunities to build broader mathematical
connections and problem-solving skills.

23
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:47,713
In contrast, JEI Math goes beyond arithmetic
to cover all five major areas of mathematics:

24
00:01:47,776 --> 00:01:52,630
numbers and operations, geometry,
measurement, data and graphs, and patterns.

25
00:01:53,330 --> 00:01:57,285
Students gradually learn the key concepts
and principles in each area and apply

26
00:01:57,335 --> 00:02:01,090
them to a variety of problems, broadening
their mathematical understanding.

27
00:02:01,690 --> 00:02:05,787
This comprehensive approach helps
students develop not only computational

28
00:02:05,843 --> 00:02:09,828
skills but also logical thinking, the
ability to recognize mathematical

29
00:02:09,884 --> 00:02:13,700
relationships, and well-rounded
mathematical problem-solving skills.

30
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:20,580
The second difference lies in how mathematical
concepts are taught and developed.

31
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:25,550
Let's first compare how
addition is introduced.

32
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:29,881
Rather than starting with numerical
equations, JEI Math introduces

33
00:02:29,938 --> 00:02:33,556
addition through concrete situations
and a variety of activities

34
00:02:33,612 --> 00:02:37,400
that help students naturally
understand its meaning and principles.

35
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,068
Students begin by counting
and combining objects, then

36
00:02:41,125 --> 00:02:44,420
gradually connect these
experiences to addition equations.

37
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:49,647
In contrast, the program B materials
reviewed introduce addition equations first,

38
00:02:49,703 --> 00:02:54,230
followed by activities using concrete
objects to explore the meaning of addition.

39
00:02:54,930 --> 00:02:58,177
This sequence places greater
emphasis on calculation procedures

40
00:02:58,228 --> 00:03:01,320
before students have fully
explored the meaning of addition.

41
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:06,373
JEI Math, on the other hand, builds
conceptual understanding through concrete

42
00:03:06,429 --> 00:03:11,178
experiences before progressing to mathematical
expressions and calculations, helping

43
00:03:11,234 --> 00:03:15,700
students develop the ability to understand
and apply mathematics independently.

44
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:20,420
A similar difference can
be seen in division.

45
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:24,344
JEI Math helps students understand
the principles of division

46
00:03:24,398 --> 00:03:27,450
through multiple approaches,
including grouping objects,

47
00:03:27,504 --> 00:03:30,610
skip-counting on a number line,
and repeated subtraction.

48
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:34,036
Through these activities,
students discover how different

49
00:03:34,085 --> 00:03:37,010
representations connect to the
same mathematical principle.

50
00:03:37,710 --> 00:03:41,187
In the program B materials reviewed,
greater emphasis is placed

51
00:03:41,242 --> 00:03:44,719
on learning calculation procedures
and practicing similar types

52
00:03:44,774 --> 00:03:47,920
of problems after introducing
the principles of division.

53
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:53,539
This systematic progression, from understanding
mathematical principles through multiple

54
00:03:53,594 --> 00:03:58,010
approaches to application and mastery,
is the second key advantage of JEI Math.

55
00:04:00,410 --> 00:04:04,500
The third and final difference lies in
the Diagnosis and Prescription System.

56
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:09,800
Math learning programs differ
in how they assess students'

57
00:04:09,850 --> 00:04:12,150
abilities and determine
their starting points.

58
00:04:12,850 --> 00:04:16,600
Program A uses test completion time
and the number of correct answers

59
00:04:16,654 --> 00:04:20,350
to identify a recommended starting
point based on a reference graph.

60
00:04:20,950 --> 00:04:23,386
The instructor then considers
their observations and

61
00:04:23,433 --> 00:04:26,150
judgment to determine the
student's actual starting point.

62
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:31,476
Meanwhile, program B determines each student's
starting level based on which questions

63
00:04:31,530 --> 00:04:35,780
they answer incorrectly, regardless of
how long they take to complete the test.

64
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:43,767
In contrast, JEI Math analyzes assessment
results from three perspectives: Analysis

65
00:04:43,835 --> 00:04:49,220
by Objectives, Analysis by Learning
Functions, and Analysis by Answer Selection.

66
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:53,812
Rather than simply identifying correct
and incorrect answers, the system

67
00:04:53,867 --> 00:04:58,029
examines which learning objectives
students have not mastered, which learning

68
00:04:58,083 --> 00:05:02,030
functions need improvement, and the
possible reasons behind their errors.

69
00:05:02,730 --> 00:05:07,162
Built around 2,619 detailed learning
objectives, the system uses these results

70
00:05:07,218 --> 00:05:11,650
to determine what each student needs to
learn and how much practice they need.

71
00:05:12,450 --> 00:05:16,920
By combining systematic learning design
with precise diagnosis and personalized

72
00:05:16,977 --> 00:05:21,730
prescriptions, JEI Math provides targeted
learning tailored to each student's needs.

73
00:05:22,330 --> 00:05:25,100
This is the third key
advantage of JEI Math.

74
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:30,641
JEI Math identifies students'
learning gaps through both

75
00:05:30,697 --> 00:05:33,950
Analysis by Objectives and
Analysis by Learning Functions.

76
00:05:34,650 --> 00:05:38,259
The first, Analysis by Objectives,
groups related assessment questions

77
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:41,610
according to their learning
objectives and analyzes the results.

78
00:05:42,210 --> 00:05:45,735
When a learning gap is identified
in a particular area, the system

79
00:05:45,788 --> 00:05:48,992
selects the appropriate Prescribed
Workbooks to address that

80
00:05:49,046 --> 00:05:52,410
gap, providing targeted learning
based on each student's needs.

81
00:05:54,810 --> 00:05:57,510
The second is Analysis
by Learning Functions.

82
00:05:58,110 --> 00:06:01,089
This system groups learning
objectives associated with the

83
00:06:01,140 --> 00:06:04,170
same learning function and
analyzes the assessment results.

84
00:06:04,770 --> 00:06:08,485
When a gap is identified in a particular
learning function, the system

85
00:06:08,538 --> 00:06:12,040
selects Prescribed Workbooks designed
to strengthen that function.

86
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:16,231
This helps identify which learning
functions students are struggling

87
00:06:16,282 --> 00:06:19,670
with and provides focused practice
to address those specific gaps.

88
00:06:22,070 --> 00:06:24,480
Next is Analysis by Answer Selection.

89
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:27,914
Even when students answer the
same problem incorrectly,

90
00:06:27,965 --> 00:06:30,490
the reasons behind their
errors may be different.

91
00:06:31,190 --> 00:06:34,388
For example, in the addition
problem 67 plus 18,

92
00:06:34,455 --> 00:06:37,920
choosing 75 may indicate
difficulty with regrouping.

93
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:42,239
Choosing 86 may suggest an
error in basic addition, while

94
00:06:42,305 --> 00:06:46,220
choosing 715 may indicate a
misunderstanding of place value.

95
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:51,869
By analyzing the incorrect answer selected,
JEI Math identifies possible causes

96
00:06:51,932 --> 00:06:56,630
of errors and prescribes workbooks to
address the underlying learning gaps.

97
00:06:57,230 --> 00:07:00,486
Instead of simply having students
repeat the problems they missed,

98
00:07:00,535 --> 00:07:03,840
the system focuses on addressing
the reasons behind their mistakes.

99
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:08,610
Even when two students
make the same number of

100
00:07:08,662 --> 00:07:11,290
errors, their learning needs
may be very different.

101
00:07:11,990 --> 00:07:16,280
For example, two students may each
answer seven questions incorrectly.

102
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:19,587
Yet one may struggle with
two-digit addition, while

103
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:22,400
the other has gaps in counting
and basic arithmetic.

104
00:07:23,100 --> 00:07:26,792
JEI Math systematically analyzes
these differences to determine

105
00:07:26,851 --> 00:07:30,250
the appropriate starting level
for each student and select

106
00:07:30,308 --> 00:07:33,590
Prescribed Workbooks tailored
to their individual needs.

107
00:07:35,990 --> 00:07:39,470
We've explored the three
key advantages of JEI Math.

108
00:07:40,170 --> 00:07:44,334
Comprehensive coverage of all five
major areas of mathematics, systematic

109
00:07:44,391 --> 00:07:48,098
learning progression from conceptual
understanding to application

110
00:07:48,155 --> 00:07:51,920
and mastery, and precise diagnosis
and personalized prescriptions.

111
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:56,880
Together, these three strengths form an
integrated learning system that supports

112
00:07:56,932 --> 00:08:00,780
each student's progress according to
their individual abilities and needs.

113
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:04,890
This is the core competitive
advantage of JEI Math.

114
00:08:07,290 --> 00:08:10,177
JEI Math provides learning
tailored to each student's

115
00:08:10,231 --> 00:08:13,118
abilities and needs, helping
students progress toward

116
00:08:13,173 --> 00:08:16,550
complete mastery through
personalized, ability-based learning.

